Definition: Coexistence Handshake — sec-04A.2 minimal-lattice-consumer formal specification

  Scope:
    - Authored at the coexistence-handshake proofs the §11 coexistence section
      first checkbox per the MS-4 mission anchor (00-overview.md MS-4: "Ori-novel
      coexistence-proof"). Single Source of Truth for the predicates, functions,
      and partition referenced by CH-1..CH-5 + CH-comp.
    - Intel: `coexistence_handshake` / `burden_registry` symbol-lookups return
      not-found (intel-query.sh similar both, 2026-05-28) — consistent with the
      MS-4 "no reference compiler has this composition" framing per 00-overview.md
      Design Principle 2 + Annex E §AIMS Prior Art Cross-Reference. Closest
      prior-art shapes: Koka Perceus FBIP-certification (function-level proof; AIMS
      operates at instruction-level) at [koka:src/Core/CheckFBIP.hs]; Lean 4 LCNF
      binary borrow inference (per-pass proof; AIMS proves per-class) at
      [lean4:src/Lean/Compiler/IR/Borrow.lean]. The coexistence composition itself
      is Ori-novel. `eliminate_burden_ops` has 29 callers (intel-query.sh callers
      eliminate_burden_ops, 2026-05-28), all under
      compiler/ori_arc/src/aims/realize/burden_elim/tests.rs (test
      fixtures, not production composition surfaces).

  Imports / dependencies:
    - Annex E §AIMS (the 7-dimension product lattice — Access §AIMS §3.1, Consumption
      §AIMS §3.2, Cardinality §AIMS §3.3, Uniqueness §AIMS §3.4, Locality §AIMS §3.5, Shape §AIMS §3.6, Effect
      §AIMS §3.7) for AimsState dimensions consumed by the formal definitions below
    - Annex E §AIMS DP-1 (`is_rc_needed`), DP-2 (`is_rc_dec_unnecessary`), DP-3
      (`is_rc_inc_elidable`), DP-9 (`cow_mode`) — the elimination-decision predicates
      consumed by `class_covered` membership
    - Annex E §AIMS IC-3 (ParamContract dimensions) — class identification per
      callee-parameter contract dimensions
    - Annex E §AIMS RL-2 (RC dec at last use / scope exit), RL-7 (dynamic COW for
      MaybeShared), RL-14 (headerless stack promotion under Locality <= FunctionLocal
      and Uniqueness = Unique) — the realization rules per AIMS class
    - aims-proof/proofs/04-transfers/TF-3.proof (Construct FRESH initialization),
      TF-4.proof (Project borrow propagation), TF-6.proof / TF-6a.proof
      (Apply/Invoke refine contract), TF-8.proof (Select scalar-exclusion join),
      TF-11.proof (backward demand propagation), TF-14.proof (Project source demand
      propagation), TF-15.proof / TF-15a.proof (Set/SetTag in-place mutation backward
      demand) — the proven calculus rules CH-1 grounds against
    - aims-proof/proofs/02-lattice/L-1..L-8.proof (lattice properties: commutativity,
      associativity, idempotence, partial order, finite height, monotonicity,
      canonicalization idempotence, canonicalization preserves joins) — substrate
      L-2/L-6 are load-bearing for CH-4 (lattice state-map immutability under
      burden-registry mutation) and CH-2 (DP-2/DP-3 elimination consumer composed
      with predicate-stack ops)
    - aims-proof/proofs/05-decisions/DP-1.proof, DP-2.proof, DP-3.proof, DP-9.proof
      — discharge the truth-tables consumed by `class_covered` membership
    - aims-proof/proofs/06-interprocedural/IC-3-param-join.proof — discharges the
      `(Borrowed | Owned) x may_share` parameter contract that classifies a
      variable's AIMS class for CH-3

  Notation:
    - lattice = converged AimsStateMap per intraprocedural backward analysis
      (IA-7), with per-variable lattice state at every program point
    - BR = burden registry, a typed pre-pass producing per-variable burden
      annotations (per docs/ori_lang/proposals/approved/aims-burden-tracking-proposal.md
      sec-04A success_criterion 4: `burden_emitted: BitSet<ArcVarId>` populated by
      `emit_burden_ops` AND `class_covered: BitSet<ClassId>` derived
      intraprocedurally in aims/intraprocedural/post_convergence.rs)
    - C = an AIMS class identified by IC-3 ParamContract dimensions (Access,
      Consumption, Cardinality, Uniqueness, Locality, may_share)
    - class_members(C) = the set of program variables (ArcVarId values) assigned
      to class C by IC-3 + intraprocedural classification
    - field_type(f) = the static type of struct field f, used to identify the AIMS
      class membership of a transitive payload

  Definition (Predicate 1): burden-owned
    burden-owned: AimsState -> Bool
    burden-owned(s) iff
        s.access = Owned (per Annex E §AIMS §3.1)
      and (s.consumption in {Linear, Affine}) (per Annex E §AIMS.2)
      and s.uniqueness = Unique (per Annex E §AIMS.4)
      and is_rc_dec_unnecessary(s) (per Annex E §AIMS DP-2)

    The conjunction is the formal lattice-bridge bridging the burden registry's
    pre-pass annotations to the lattice's converged AimsStateMap entries. A
    variable v's converged lattice state L[v] satisfies burden-owned IFF the
    burden registry's elimination decision (DP-2 / DP-3) is consistent with the
    lattice's per-variable claim, NOT independent of it.

  Definition (Predicate 2): class_covered
    class_covered: Type x BurdenRegistry -> Bool

    Per the sec-11 success_criterion 1 mixed-coverage projection-boundary + field-grain
    dispatch rule (addresses the partial-coverage gap in mixed class coverage):

    class_covered(C, BR) iff
      (Forall v in class_members(C). burden-owned(L[v]) and v in BR.burden_emitted)
      and (Forall f in fields(C). class_covered(field_type(f), BR))
      (transitive payload closure — mirrors aims-burden-tracking sec-04A.4
       coexistence handshake class-coverage rule)

    Mixed-coverage field-grain dispatch (CRITICAL — the partial-coverage cure
    per sec-11 success_criterion 1):
      When Exists field f in fields(C). notclass_covered(field_type(f), BR), the parent C
      is NOT class_covered as a whole, but each individual field f of C carries
      its own class_covered(field_type(f), BR) bit; dispatch routes per-field to
      burden_emission_path when the field is class_covered ELSE to
      predicate_stack_path.

      Projection boundaries (TF-4 Project per sec-3 / aims-proof/proofs/04-transfers/TF-4.proof)
      inherit the field's dispatch decision, NOT the parent's. Specifically, for
      `%dst = Project %src.f`, the dispatch decision is class_covered(field_type(f),
      BR), NOT class_covered(type_of(src), BR).

  Definition (Function 1): burden_emission_path
    burden_emission_path: ArcFunction x AimsStateMap x BurdenSpec -> ArcFunction

    The sec-03-sec-04A + sec-04A.2 elimination consumer, terminating at the shipped
    `eliminate_burden_ops` function (compiler/ori_arc/src/aims/realize/
    burden_elim.rs:87 — verified `pub(crate) fn eliminate_burden_ops` per intel-query
    callers eliminate_burden_ops 2026-05-28; 29 callers all in
    compiler/ori_arc/src/aims/realize/burden_elim/tests.rs test
    fixtures, confirming there is no production composition surface ABOVE
    `eliminate_burden_ops` that this Handshake.proof must include).

    Pipeline-ordering: `emit_burden_ops` invoked between Step 4 (`analyze_function`)
    and Step 5 (`realize_rc_reuse`) per docs/ori_lang/proposals/approved/aims-burden-tracking-proposal.mdsection-04A
    success_criterion 1 (Annex E §AIMS PL-2: Step 4 precedes Step 5). The
    elimination consumer reads BR (write-once at burden-emit) AND L (read-only
    after IA-7 convergence). PL-1 interprocedural-first invariant preserved
    (CH-5 discharges this).

  Definition (Function 2): predicate_stack_path
    predicate_stack_path: ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction

    The pre-burden baseline: the sec-03-sec-04 lattice-only emission path operating
    purely on L without consulting BR. Realization rules per Annex E §AIMS
    RL-1..RL-34. This is the path Ori shipped BEFORE the sec-04A burden-emit pre-pass
    landed — the parent baseline. CH-1 grounds against the soundness of this path
    (RL-1, RL-2 composition under IA-5 step 1 alias-demand accumulation, per
    Annex E §AIMS §8 sec-08
    RL-1-RL-2-composition.proof).

  Definition (Function 3): coexistence_dispatch
    coexistence_dispatch: ArcFunction x AimsStateMap x BurdenSpec x C -> ArcFunction

    The dispatch decision per the soundness theorem decomposition (sec-11
    success_criterion 2 partition):

      case 1 (class_covered):
        if class_covered(C, BR):
          return burden_emission_path(F, L, BR) o predicate_stack_path(F, L)
          (per the sec-11 success_criterion 2 Case 1 soundness theorem statement:
           coexistence_dispatch is observably equivalent to BOTH paths — both
           run, their effects compose, and the lattice state-map remains
           invariant under the burden-registry mutation per CH-4)

      case 2 (mixed-coverage):
        if notclass_covered(C, BR) and Exists f in fields(C). class_covered(field_type(f), BR):
          for each f in fields(C):
            if class_covered(field_type(f), BR):
              dispatch field f via burden_emission_path
            else:
              dispatch field f via predicate_stack_path
          (per the sec-11 success_criterion 2 Case 2 soundness theorem statement:
           per-field dispatch composes via sec-07 PL-3 emission-order; observable
           equivalence to predicate_stack_path under the projection-boundary +
           field-grain access dispatch rule)

      case 3 (uncovered):
        if notclass_covered(C, BR) and Forall f in fields(C). notclass_covered(field_type(f), BR):
          return predicate_stack_path(F, L)
          (per the sec-11 success_criterion 2 Case 3 soundness theorem statement:
           by definition, no burden_emission_path branch taken; coexistence_dispatch
           equivalent_to predicate_stack_path)

  Definition (Partition): the burden-path vs predicate-stack-path partition
    The variable space vars(F) of any ArcFunction F is partitioned by
    class_covered into three disjoint subsets:

      vars(F) = BurdenCovered(F, BR) disjoint_union MixedCoverage(F, BR) disjoint_union Uncovered(F, BR)

    where:
      BurdenCovered(F, BR) = { v in vars(F) | class_covered(class_of(v), BR) }
      MixedCoverage(F, BR) = { v in vars(F) | notclass_covered(class_of(v), BR)
                                            and Exists f. class_covered(field_type(f), BR) }
      Uncovered(F, BR) = { v in vars(F) | notclass_covered(class_of(v), BR)
                                            and Forall f. notclass_covered(field_type(f), BR) }

    Totality + disjointness:
      Forall v in vars(F). v in BurdenCovered(F, BR) XOR v in MixedCoverage(F, BR)
                       XOR v in Uncovered(F, BR)
      (CH-3 discharges this — per-class coexistence three sub-classes are
       total + disjoint at the lattice level per Annex E §AIMS product lattice
       L-9 SCALAR-exclusion + L-5 finite height + L-7 canonicalization idempotence)

  Soundness theorem (Coexistence Handshake Soundness):
    Forall ArcFunction F. Forall AimsStateMap L. Forall BurdenSpec BR. Forall class C.

      coexistence_dispatch(F, L, BR, C) produces observably equivalent behavior
      to the case-specific path per the partition above:

        case 1: equivalent_to burden_emission_path(F, L, BR) AND equivalent_to predicate_stack_path(F, L)
                (the layered-composition union-coverage semantics — both paths
                observable, both consistent with L, no double-counting per CH-1)

        case 2: equivalent_to predicate_stack_path(F, L) under per-field dispatch
                (projection-boundary + field-grain access dispatch rule;
                sec-07 PL-3 emission-order composes per-field decisions)

        case 3: equivalent_to predicate_stack_path(F, L)
                (by definition; coexistence_dispatch trivially reduces)

    The theorem is decomposed into six CH-N theorems (CH-1 through CH-5 +
    CH-comp) per the §11 coexistence section Per-CH Proof-Status Tracking — each discharged
    individually under proof_search_cap: 5 per 00-overview Design Principle 3.

  Cross-references:
    - CH-1.proof — Burden-registry-lattice composition soundness; the root
      theorem grounding all dispatch decisions via the burden-owned lattice
      bridge (this Handshake's Predicate 1).
    - CH-2.proof — DP-2/DP-3 elimination consumer composition with
      predicate-stack-derived ops; discharges single-elimination invariant
      (no double-counting) per Predicate 2's class_covered membership.
    - CH-3.proof — Per-class coexistence three sub-classes (OwnedxLinearxOnce
      xUnique RL-2+RL-14, BorrowedxLinearxOncexUnique RL-14 headerless,
      MaybeSharedxMany RL-7 dynamic COW); discharges the partition's
      totality + disjointness invariant.
    - CH-4.proof — AimsStateMap immutability under burden-registry mutation;
      discharges the read-only invariant of L w.r.t. BR mutation events (BR
      reads L; L does not depend on BR).
    - CH-5.proof — Phase-ordering composition; PL-1 interprocedural-first
      with burden-registry as Step 1 typed pre-pass (per Annex E §AIMS
      PL-2). Discharges CH-4's BR-reads-L acyclic-dependency proof.
    - CH-comp.proof — CH-1..CH-5 union-soundness composition mirroring sec-09
      VF-comp.proof pattern (a fix passing a strict subset of CH-N is
      rejected; 5-count + composition coverage gate prevents a dropped CH
      layer).

  Expected:
    status: definition_only
    reason: this file is the formal-specification SSOT consumed by CH-1..CH-5
      + CH-comp; it carries no proof obligation of its own. CH-1.proof
      (authored alongside) discharges the first soundness theorem against
      this Handshake's Predicate 1 + Function 1 + Function 2 + Function 3
      definitions; subsequent CH-N proofs ground against the same SSOT.
